   - **1980s Bridges**: Utilized **modern materials** like **high-performance concrete**, **stainless steel**, and **advanced composites**. These materials are more resistant to environmental stressors and have longer lifespans. The 1980s also saw the adoption of **computer-aided design (CAD)** and **precision engineering**, resulting in more precise and durable structures.

